<%# R7.2. The reader is waiting, so show something moving and say something calm.

    started-at comes from the server because polling replaces this whole page
    every couple of seconds, tearing the Stimulus controller down and building it
    again — measured at five rebuilds in nine seconds. Anything the controller
    remembers resets that often, so the elapsed time has to come from outside it.
    The spinner's one-second cycle divides evenly into the two-second poll, so it
    lands on the same phase each time and reads as continuous. %>
<div data-controller="processing"
     data-processing-slow-after-value="20000"
     data-processing-interval-value="2000"
     data-processing-started-at-value="<%= current_insurance_session.analyzing_since&.to_i %>">

  <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
    <%# Decorative: the status is carried by the live region below, so a screen
        reader should not announce this. Held still for readers who ask for
        reduced motion. %>
    <span class="inline-block h-8 w-8 shrink-0 rounded-full border-4 border-rule border-t-accent motion-safe:animate-spin"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <h1 class="text-title font-bold">Reading your document…</h1>
  </div>

  <p class="text-lead mb-8" data-processing-target="message" aria-live="polite">
    This usually takes a few seconds.
  </p>

  <p class="text-body text-ink-muted hidden" data-processing-target="slow" aria-live="polite">
    This is taking a little longer than usual. We're still working on it.
  </p>

  <%# Without JavaScript the page still moves forward, just less smoothly. %>
  <noscript>
    <p class="text-body"><%= link_to "Check if it is ready", root_path, class: "text-accent" %></p>
  </noscript>
</div>
